{"archetypes":[{"name":"repo-validation-consistency","focus_area":"correctness","weight":2,"rationale":"validate_repo is now copy-pasted across ~7 scripts with identical regex; any one diverging silently breaks the security invariant.","prompt_body":"Verify that the validate_repo function (regex ^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$ plus case-statement prefix checks) is textually identical in every script that defines it: clarify-comment-post.sh, clarify-label.sh, clarify-state.sh, named-block-write.sh, design-log-publish.sh, design-pause-save.sh, and design-pause-load.sh (validate_repo_value variant). Flag any divergence in allowed characters, path-prefix rules, or the regex. Also check whether the two-phase validate-then-resolve pattern (validate argv REPO_ARG before source-env.sh, then re-validate after resolve_repo) is consistently applied across all callers that take both an argv --repo and a resolved fallback. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"source-env-awk-extraction","focus_area":"correctness","weight":2,"rationale":"design-pause-save.sh replaced source source-env.sh with awk-based key extraction; the awk parser must handle all printf '%q' quoted value shapes that write-design-current-env.sh produces.","prompt_body":"Review the source_env_get awk function added to scripts/design-pause-save.sh. The function extracts SESSION_ID and REPO from source-env.sh by parsing 'export KEY=value' lines. Check whether it correctly handles all value shapes produced by printf '%q' output (e.g., single-quoted values like 'owner/repo', values with hyphens, empty values, values with embedded spaces). Verify the awk single-quote character construction (sprintf(\"%c\", 39)) is correct on macOS Bash 3.2 awk. Check whether REPO_ARG precedence-over-source-env logic at lines ~856-858 correctly preserves an already-validated REPO_ARG even when source-env exports a different REPO. Confirm that SESSION_ID extraction does not accidentally overwrite a caller-supplied SESSION_ID environment variable. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"contradictory-envelope-normalization","focus_area":"code-robustness","weight":2,"rationale":"The narrowed design-pause-save.sh fail-closed branch (non-zero exit + PUBLISH_OK=true) now clears RECOVERY_BRANCH; a post-push failure with a real recovery branch could have PUBLISH_OK=true in the stdout if design-log-publish.sh has a bug — verify that path does not inadvertently discard the recovery branch.","prompt_body":"In scripts/design-pause-save.sh, verify the new contradictory-envelope block (lines that check publish_rc -ne 0 AND PUBLISH_OK==true) correctly nulls out RECOVERY_BRANCH before falling through to the existing PUBLISH_OK != true branch. Confirm the existing PUBLISH_OK != true block still uses the (now cleared) RECOVERY_BRANCH to route to publish-and-recovery-failed vs recovery-branch paths, and that this new clearing cannot accidentally discard a valid RECOVERY_BRANCH=larch-log-design-<RUN_ID> from a legitimate post-push failure where design-log-publish.sh might emit exit 1 + PUBLISH_OK=false + RECOVERY_BRANCH. Also check the pause-state.txt redaction-and-copy sequence: the second cp redacted_state_tmp -> pause-state.txt after the PUBLISH_OK != true block appears to re-overwrite the first cp; confirm this is intentional and correct. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"emit-fail-cleanup-side-effect","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"emit_fail in design-pause-save.sh now unconditionally removes .pause-requested before emitting PAUSE_OK=false; removing it on tmpdir-unset, invalid-issue, or invalid-run-id paths where DESIGN_TMPDIR may be empty or unvalidated could silently succeed against a wrong path.","prompt_body":"In scripts/design-pause-save.sh, the updated emit_fail function conditionally removes $DESIGN_TMPDIR/.pause-requested before emitting PAUSE_OK=false. Check whether the guard condition ([[ -n \"${DESIGN_TMPDIR:-}\" && -d \"$DESIGN_TMPDIR\" ]] && larch_design_tmpdir_validate) is sufficient to prevent the rm from running against an unvalidated or user-controlled DESIGN_TMPDIR value — specifically for error paths called before the main [[ -n \"$DESIGN_TMPDIR\" ]] || emit_fail check (e.g., invalid-repo emitted immediately after argv parse). Verify that larch_design_tmpdir_validate cannot be fooled by a path that satisfies -d but is not a legitimate session tmpdir. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"publish-skipped-outcome-completeness","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"publish-skipped is added to render-run-summary.sh and docs but the diff does not show render-final-summary.sh changes, which the plan says should also add the outcome; missing from the diff may indicate an incomplete implementation.","prompt_body":"The plan says render-final-summary.sh should add publish-skipped to its outcome case enum and honest Publish-skipped note, and compose_self_fallback should also match it. Check whether the diff includes changes to skills/design/scripts/render-final-summary.sh matching these requirements. If those changes are absent from the diff, check whether render-final-summary.sh already handles publish-skipped through a wildcard match or whether it would exit 2 on an unknown outcome. Also verify that design-publish.sh SUMMARY_OUTCOME selection in the diff correctly sets publish-skipped when SESSION_ID is empty, and approved/failed-publish otherwise. Cross-check that the test-render-final-summary.sh changes claimed in the plan are present in the diff. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
